from pages10 import notice
PAGES=[
notice('instagram-we-limit-how-often-notice','Instagram','We limit how often you can do certain things','“We Limit How Often You Can Do Certain Things” on Instagram (2026)','This is an action block, not a ban. Instagram paused some actions, such as following, liking, commenting or sending messages, because the activity looked automated or too fast.','<strong>“We limit how often you can do certain things” is a temporary action block, not a disabled account.</strong> Stop the blocked action, remove third-party apps that automate likes or follows, and change your password. Use the “Tell us” option once if you think it is a mistake. Instagram makes the final decision.',['Stop the blocked action for now.','Remove any app that automates follows, likes or DMs.','Change your password and log out of unknown devices.','Use the “Tell us” option once if it was a mistake.'],[('Is this a ban?','No. It limits some actions for a while. Repeating the action can make the limit longer.'),('How long does it last?','Instagram does not share a set length, and it varies.')]),
notice('facebook-your-account-is-restricted-right-now-notice','Facebook','Your account is restricted right now','“Your Account Is Restricted Right Now” on Facebook: What It Means (2026)','Facebook limited some features, such as posting, commenting, messaging or joining groups, often for a set period. The profile itself is still active.','<strong>“Your account is restricted right now” on Facebook means some features are paused, not that the profile is disabled.</strong> Open Account Status to see which rule and how long. If you disagree, use the review option there once. Meta makes the final decision.',['Open Account Status in settings.','Read which rule and which features are limited.','Use the disagree option once if it was a mistake.','Avoid the limited action until the end date.'],[('Is restricted the same as disabled?','No. Restricted limits some features. Disabled turns the profile off.'),('Where do I see the end date?','In Account Status, if Facebook shows one.')]),
notice('instagram-your-account-may-be-deleted-notice','Instagram','Your account may be deleted','“Your Account May Be Deleted” on Instagram: What to Do (2026)','Instagram warns that the account has broken rules several times and may be removed if it happens again. The account still works for now.','<strong>“Your account may be deleted” is a warning, not a deletion.</strong> Open Account Status, read which posts or actions were flagged, and avoid repeating them. If a removal was a mistake, request a review for that item. Instagram makes the final decision.',['Open Account Status in settings.','Review the flagged posts or actions.','Request a review for any removal you think was a mistake.','Avoid repeating the flagged activity.'],[('Has my account been deleted?','No. This is a warning. The account still works.'),('Can I clear the warnings?','Some violations expire over time. Instagram decides how long.')]),
]
